---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Rules Overview" description="SpaceAge Rules - Core Game Mechanics">
  <section class="rules-content">
	<h1>Rules Overview</h1>

	<div class="intro-card card">
	  <h2>How SpaceAge Works</h2>
	  <p>
		SpaceAge is a quarterly turn-based strategy game. Each turn simulates 13 weeks of in-game time.
		You control an Interest (faction) pursuing your own strategic goals across the galaxy.
	  </p>
	</div>

	<section class="core-concepts">
	  <h2>Core Concepts</h2>

	  <div class="concept-card card">
		<h3>📍 The Galaxy & Points</h3>
		<p>
		  The game world is a network of star systems connected by ancient Points — stable wormholes that enable
		  faster-than-light travel. These Points form in the outer reaches of star systems (the <strong>Alderson Corona</strong>),
		  far enough to avoid tidal destruction but close enough to form in the star's gravity well.
		</p>
		<p>
		  In a single catastrophic day, the Points shut down. Commerce died. Colonies starved. After four months, most
		  reopened — but not all connections were restored. Some systems remain isolated. And two Points that led to
		  Earth stayed dark, leaving only mystery and fear.
		</p>
	  </div>

	  <div class="concept-card card">
		<h3>🚀 Interests & Factions</h3>
		<p>
		  You are an <strong>Interest</strong> — a corporation, fleet, association, or any other entity with strategic ambitions.
		  In this campaign, ten Interests (factions 2–11) compete and cooperate across the stars. NPC factions (1, 12, 13)
		  also exist in the world but do not submit player orders.
		</p>
		<p>
		  There is no forced victory condition. You set your own goals: colonization, exploration, trade, science, or warfare.
		</p>
	  </div>

	  <div class="concept-card card">
		<h3>⏰ Quarterly Turns</h3>
		<p>
		  One game turn = one quarter = 13 weeks of in-game time. You read a quarterly report, analyze what happened,
		  discuss strategy (via Discord, email, or forums), and submit orders. The game master processes the turn and
		  publishes new reports. This cycle repeats.
		</p>
		<p>
		  Because turns take time to discuss and process, a single quarter of in-game time may span a week or more of real time.
		</p>
	  </div>

	  <div class="concept-card card">
		<h3>🛸 Units & Resources</h3>
		<p>
		  Your faction controls ships (scouts, freighters, warships), facilities (mines, labs, shipyards), resources (metals,
		  rare elements, fuel), and trained personnel (commanders, scientists, engineers). Each resource has costs and benefits.
		  Strategic choices about what to build, explore, or attack shape your long-term success.
		</p>
	  </div>

	  <div class="concept-card card">
		<h3>🔬 Research & Technology</h3>
		<p>
		  A 10-level technology tree defines what you can build and research. Early techs (level 0–2) are basic and cheap.
		  Higher levels unlock better ships, weapons, and modules — but require significant research investment and resources.
		  Technology choices define your faction's capabilities and playstyle.
		</p>
	  </div>

	  <div class="concept-card card">
		<h3>⚔️ Combat & Tactics</h3>
		<p>
		  When interests clash, combat is resolved by the engine. Weapon types (kinetic, missile, energy) have different
		  advantages and disadvantages. Ships with armor, shields, and trained crews have better survivability. Tactics matter:
		  you can choose to destroy enemies, capture their ships, or attempt to evade.
		</p>
	  </div>
	</section>

	<section class="gameplay-flow">
	  <h2>Gameplay Flow</h2>
	  <ol class="flow-list">
		<li>
		  <strong>Receive Report:</strong> At the start of a turn, you get a detailed report of your faction's status,
		  including units, locations, resources, and research progress.
		</li>
		<li>
		  <strong>Plan Strategy:</strong> Analyze the report and discuss with allies or opponents. Decide your next moves.
		</li>
		<li>
		  <strong>Write Orders:</strong> Specify actions for your ships, facilities, and personnel. Orders use a text-based
		  syntax and can be drafted in the visual tool client.
		</li>
		<li>
		  <strong>Submit Orders:</strong> Send your order file to the game master before the deadline.
		</li>
		<li>
		  <strong>Processing:</strong> The GM collects all orders and runs the engine to simulate the quarter.
		</li>
		<li>
		  <strong>New Reports:</strong> The engine outputs new faction reports reflecting all the actions and results.
		</li>
		<li>
		  <strong>Repeat:</strong> The cycle continues for the next quarter.
		</li>
	  </ol>
	</section>

	<section class="sample-orders">
	  <h2>Sample Orders</h2>
	  <div class="card">
		<p>
		  Orders control what your units do each turn: moving ships between systems, researching technology, mining resources,
		  building new units, engaging in combat, or diplomacy. The exact syntax and options are documented in the full
		  <strong>Player Rules</strong> (available in the client and linked below).
		</p>
		<p style="font-size: var(--font-size-sm); color: #999; margin-top: var(--space-lg);">
		  Sample orders and detailed order syntax are in the full rules document.
		</p>
	  </div>
	</section>

	<section class="full-rules-section card">
	  <h2>Full Rules & Documentation</h2>
	  <p>
		This overview covers the basics. For detailed rules, order syntax, technology tree, combat formulas, and more,
		consult the complete <strong>Player Rules</strong> document (available in the game client or on this site).
	  </p>
	  <p>
		<strong>Questions?</strong> Check the <a href="/">home page</a> or ask the game master on the campaign's community channel.
	  </p>
	</section>

	<section class="design-philosophy card">
	  <h2>Design Philosophy</h2>
	  <p>
		SpaceAge follows the tradition of open PBEM strategy games: hard science (wormholes, orbital mechanics, resource constraints),
		no forced narrative, and player agency. Your decisions matter. Diplomacy, deception, and strategy are as valid as military might.
		There is no single path to success — only the path your Interest chooses.
	  </p>
	</section>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .rules-content {
	max-width: 900px;
	margin: 0 auto;
  }

  h1 {
	color: var(--color-accent-teal);
	margin-bottom: var(--space-xl);
  }

  .intro-card {
	margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .core-concepts {
	margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .concept-card {
	margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .concept-card h3 {
	color: var(--color-accent-teal);
	margin-top: 0;
  }

  .gameplay-flow {
	margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .flow-list {
	margin-left: var(--space-lg);
	line-height: 2;
  }

  .flow-list li {
	margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .sample-orders {
	margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .full-rules-section {
	margin-bottom: var(--space-2xl);
  }

  .design-philosophy {
	background-color: rgba(13, 148, 136, 0.05);
	border: 1px solid var(--color-accent-teal);
  }

  a {
	color: var(--color-accent-teal);
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
	.concept-card {
	  margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
	}
  }
</style>
